<title>USA: Hi-Tech says generic minoxidil approved.</title>
<headline>Hi-Tech says generic minoxidil approved.</headline>
<dateline>AMITYVILLE, N.Y. 1996-12-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hi-Tech Pharmacal Co Inc said on Monday it has received U.S. Food and Drug Administration marketing approval for Minoxidil Topical Solution 2 percent, which is the generic version of Pharmacia &amp; Upjohn Inc's Rogaine.</p>
<p>Rogaine is used to treat hair loss, the company said.</p>
<p>Hi-Tech Pharmacal said the approval is its seventh for 1996.</p>
</text>
